An ingest whose final fdatasync fails, with no memory to publish the degraded
state, throws std::bad_alloc in the I/O error's place. Reverts #618.
Guarded-by: "alloc sweep: ingest whose fdatasync fails"

diff --git a/bytecaskdb/db_replication.cpp b/bytecaskdb/db_replication.cpp
index 8b83e51..a44d7ac 100644
--- a/bytecaskdb/db_replication.cpp
+++ b/bytecaskdb/db_replication.cpp
@@ -444,7 +444,8 @@ void DB::ingest(const ChangeHeader &header,
       t.active_file().sync();
       t.apply_sync(t.next_seq() - 1);
     } catch (...) {
-      degrade_from(current, "ingest fdatasync failed: call resume() to recover.");
+      store_state(current->degraded_copy(
+          "ingest fdatasync failed: call resume() to recover."));
       throw;
     }
 
